---
import Page from "../layouts/page.astro";
---

<style>
	article {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--spacing-l);
	}
	ul {
		margin-top: var(--spacing-m);
		padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
	}
	li {
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-m);
	}

	.employer {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: baseline;
	}
	.employer-name {
		font-weight: bold;
	}
	.employer-meta {
		color: var(--muted-color);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.role {
		margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-m);
		color: var(--muted-color);
	}
	.note {
		font-style: italic;
		margin-top: var(--spacing-s);
		margin-bottom: 0;
		color: var(--muted-color);
	}
</style>

<Page title="Resume">
	<article>
		<a
			href="/resume.pdf"
			download="Timothy Hall - Resume.pdf"
			role="button"
			class="outline"
		>
			Download PDF
		</a>

		<section>
			<div class="employer">
				<span class="employer-name">Postman</span>
				<span class="employer-meta"
					>Working Remotely | February 2022 – Present</span
				>
			</div>
			<p class="role">Technical Lead</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Leading the development of Postman's next runtime, the core that
					powers all of Postman. Executes collections and requests of all types
					using a plugin-driven approach that makes it simple to add new
					low-level functionality to Postman, while reliably sending 100+
					million requests every week
				</li>
				<li>
					Led the development of Postman's new GraphQL client, building an
					advanced query builder, schema documentation and explorer, and fast
					schema search that integrated as simple and useful tooling for end
					users
					<p class="note">
						Presented "Building Tooling That Speaks GraphQL" at GraphQLConf 2023
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					Created a foundation of accessible, composable, and reusable
					components and systems that are applied to multiple workbenches,
					including HTTP, gRPC, and GraphQL
				</li>
				<li>
					Implemented improvements to the first time user flow to simplify and
					beautify the landing screen, demonstrate the benefits of signing up,
					and smooth the sign up experience that led to 50,000 more users
					signing up every week
				</li>
				<li>
					Modeled complex interactions in React using state machines, context,
					signals, and other advanced state management approaches
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<div class="employer">
				<span class="employer-name">Capital One</span>
				<span class="employer-meta"
					>Richmond, VA | July 2019 – February 2022</span
				>
			</div>
			<p class="role">Master Software Developer</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Tech Lead driving the architecture and design of UI products for
					enterprise payments used across Capital One
				</li>
				<li>
					Ensured the product and technical design smoothly grew from a small
					team to multiple teams working in parallel while keeping the product,
					and teams that built it, performant and reliable
				</li>
				<li>
					Developed a backend system with GraphQL that intelligently spread
					complex queries across multiple systems, including PostgreSQL,
					Elasticsearch, and REST endpoints
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="role">Senior Software Developer</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Developed reusable components and tooling as part of the Design System
					team that supported the entire Commercial organization within Capital
					One
				</li>
				<li>
					Discovered common patterns and needs from community feedback and
					suggestions, created accessible components in Angular and React, and
					ensured they were well-documented, tested, and useful before releasing
					them to the organization
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<div class="employer">
				<span class="employer-name">Cornerstone Systems NW</span>
				<span class="employer-meta"
					>Working Remotely | May 2013 – June 2019</span
				>
			</div>
			<p class="role">Software Developer</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Work collaboratively as part of a remote team of developers on large
					React, d3, and Backbone.js applications, developing advanced systems
					that condense information and tasks into focused, simple interfaces
				</li>
				<li>
					Lead a developer experience initiative that unified and modernized
					internal build tooling, testing, and development processes to aid
					sharing across teams, improve code quality, and increase iteration
					speed
				</li>
				<li>
					Create composable and configurable charting system that dramatically
					simplifies the process of creating new visualizations and allows rapid
					iteration of chart design and layout
					<p class="note">
						See d3-composer for details: <a
							href="https://github.com/CSNW/d3-composer"
							>github.com/CSNW/d3-composer</a
						>
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					Design and build an asynchronous data layer for working with csv data,
					including querying, caching, and advanced processing
				</li>
				<li>
					Create a reusable component library with React, Backbone, and d3
					components for bootstrapping new projects and sharing best practices
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</article>
</Page>
